WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:21.730
"Look!" Maggie cried. "Do you think that's the van?"

2
00:00:21.731 --> 00:00:26.340
Henry looked up from tying his shoelace.

3
00:00:26.341 --> 00:00:30.607
His cousin, Maggie, was jumping up and down and pointing down the street.

4
00:00:30.608 --> 00:00:35.544
"William said that his parents were sending a blue van to pick us up," Henry said.

5
00:00:35.545 --> 00:00:37.428
"That must be the one."

6
00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:40.176
Cole grabbed his backpack off the sidewalk.

7
00:00:40.177 --> 00:00:44.041
"I can't wait to get to the beach!" he exclaimed.

8
00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:46.831
"Me neither," Henry agreed.

9
00:00:46.832 --> 00:00:52.496
Their new friend, William, had invited the three of them to spend the weekend at his family's beach house.

10
00:00:52.497 --> 00:00:57.975
It was on an island located about an hour's drive from Belltown, where they all lived.

11
00:00:57.976 --> 00:01:03.087
The van stopped at the curb. A young woman was driving.

12
00:01:03.088 --> 00:01:07.405
"Are you Henry, Maggie, and Cole?" she asked in a friendly voice.

13
00:01:07.406 --> 00:01:10.943
"That's them!" someone called out from the back of the van.

14
00:01:10.944 --> 00:01:12.856
"Get in here, you guys!"

15
00:01:12.857 --> 00:01:15.823
A second later the side door slid open.

16
00:01:15.824 --> 00:01:19.114
"Hi, Nathan," Henry said to the kid inside.

17
00:01:19.115 --> 00:01:24.117
Nathan lived nearby and was one of the friendliest and happiest kids Henry knew.

18
00:01:24.118 --> 00:01:27.167
He was going to William's vacation house too.

19
00:01:27.168 --> 00:01:31.874
"This is going to be great!" Cole said as he climbed into the van.

20
00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:38.312
Maggie climbed in after him. "Yeah," she agreed.

21
00:01:38.313 --> 00:01:42.706
"But I wish I didn't have to close the lemonade stand for the whole weekend."

22
00:01:42.707 --> 00:01:46.697
Cole made a face. "Are you kidding?" he said.

23
00:01:46.698 --> 00:01:51.528
"I'd much rather spend the weekend at the beach than pouring lemonade."

24
00:01:51.529 --> 00:01:54.087
"Me too," Maggie said.

25
00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:57.784
"But I could make a lot of money selling lemonade this weekend.

26
00:01:57.785 --> 00:01:59.968
And I'm saving up right now.

27
00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:05.976
My barn is having a horse show at the end of the summer, and it costs a lot to compete in the show."

28
00:02:05.977 --> 00:02:09.513
"You should have plenty of money for that," Cole said.

29
00:02:09.514 --> 00:02:12.545
"Our detective business has been booming lately.

30
00:02:12.546 --> 00:02:16.868
We solved the mystery of the missing baseball glove for Tiny last week."

31
00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:24.061
Henry nodded. "And we helped Mr. Metz find his relatives' addresses so he could plan a family reunion.

32
00:02:24.062 --> 00:02:28.173
He paid us double our usual fee for that, remember?"

33
00:02:28.174 --> 00:02:30.966
"I guess you're right."

34
00:02:30.967 --> 00:02:36.030
Maggie stared out the window, still thinking about the lemonade stand as the van pulled away.

35
00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:38.639
"Anyway, we'll be back on Monday.

36
00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.442
I hope everybody in Belltown is still thirsty when we get back."

37
00:02:42.443 --> 00:02:45.692
Cole shrugged and then turned to Nathan and Henry.

38
00:02:45.693 --> 00:02:50.144
"Do you think we'll get to go surfing at William's beach house?" he wondered.

39
00:02:50.145 --> 00:02:55.689
"I don't know," Nathan said. "I talked to William on the phone yesterday.

40
00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.260
But I didn't get to ask him many questions about this weekend.

41
00:02:59.261 --> 00:03:01.380
He sounded kind of weird."

42
00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:05.889
"He sounded weird?" Henry said. "What do you mean?"

43
00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:09.612
"He was quieter than usual." Nathan looked worried.

44
00:03:09.613 --> 00:03:12.014
"I hope he's not getting sick."

45
00:03:12.015 --> 00:03:16.024
"Was he coughing and sneezing on the phone?" asked Cole.

46
00:03:16.025 --> 00:03:22.045
"No. But my sister Nora has a really bad cold right now," Nathan said.

47
00:03:22.046 --> 00:03:24.319
"I guess that's what made me think of it."

48
00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:30.491
"Let's talk about all the fun stuff we're going to do at the beach!" Maggie said, changing the subject.

49
00:03:30.492 --> 00:03:35.750
"Yeah," Cole agreed. "Like swimming and bodysurfing . . ."

50
00:03:35.751 --> 00:03:41.977
"Maybe we can do pirate things," Nathan suggested. "Pirates are cool!"

51
00:03:41.978 --> 00:03:48.544
"I want to build a sand castle," Maggie said. "And look for seashells."

52
00:03:48.545 --> 00:03:56.024
Henry grinned. "I can't wait to do all that stuff!"

53
00:03:56.025 --> 00:03:59.628
"Here we are," the van driver said an hour later.

54
00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:04.741
Henry looked out the window. They were approaching a large, fancy house.

55
00:04:04.742 --> 00:04:11.971
It sat near a sandy beach and was bigger than Henry's house and Maggie's house put together.

56
00:04:11.972 --> 00:04:16.194
In the distance Henry could see a long row of tall, rocky cliffs.

57
00:04:16.195 --> 00:04:20.400
"Wow, this place is great!" Maggie exclaimed.

58
00:04:20.401 --> 00:04:22.812
"We're going to have so much fun."

59
00:04:22.813 --> 00:04:25.869
"Look, there's William." Nathan pointed.

60
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.246
A kid was standing in front of the house.

61
00:04:28.247 --> 00:04:31.007
A girl around his age was beside him.

62
00:04:31.008 --> 00:04:35.322
As soon as the driver stopped the van, Henry and the others jumped out.

63
00:04:35.323 --> 00:04:39.546
"Hi, William," Henry said. "Thanks for inviting us!"

64
00:04:39.547 --> 00:04:43.815
"You're welcome," William said. He pointed to the girl.

65
00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:47.653
"This is Anna. She lives here in Sea Cove."

66
00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:54.393
"You live at the beach all year long? Cool!" said Cole. "I'm Cole."

67
00:04:54.394 --> 00:05:00.493
"And I'm Henry," Henry said. "That's my cousin, Maggie, and that's Nathan."

68
00:05:00.494 --> 00:05:06.021
"Nice to meet you," Anna said. "Is this your first time coming to—"

69
00:05:06.022 --> 00:05:11.305
Suddenly a figure, waving a long, gleaming sword, leaped from behind a shrub.

70
00:05:11.306 --> 00:05:14.016
"Aargh!" he growled.
